{"type":"standard","title":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mariannette Miller-Meeks</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q58495662","titles":{"canonical":"Mariannette_Miller-Meeks","normalized":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mariannette Miller-Meeks</span></span>"},"pageid":59038656,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Mariannette_Miller-Meeks_117th_U.S_Congress.jpg/330px-Mariannette_Miller-Meeks_117th_U.S_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/54/Mariannette_Miller-Meeks_117th_U.S_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1638,"height":2048},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1375525079","tid":"6391b295-b33f-11f1-84e0-71082d004b19","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09:00:26Z","description":"American physician and politician (born 1955)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariannette_Miller-Meeks","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariannette_Miller-Meeks?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariannette_Miller-Meeks?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mariannette_Miller-Meeks"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariannette_Miller-Meeks","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Mariannette_Miller-Meeks","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariannette_Miller-Meeks?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mariannette_Miller-Meeks"}},"extract":"Mariannette Jane Miller-Meeks is an American physician and politician who has served as a U.S. representative from Iowa since 2021. Her district, numbered the 2nd from 2021 to 2023 and the 1st since 2023, includes most of Iowa's southeastern quadrant, including Davenport, Bettendorf, Burlington, and Iowa City. Previously, Miller-Meeks served as in the Iowa Senate from 2019 to 2021. She is a member of the Republican Party.","extract_html":"<p><b>Mariannette Jane Miller-Meeks</b> is an American physician and politician who has served as a U.S. representative from Iowa since 2021. Her district, numbered the 2nd from 2021 to 2023 and the 1st since 2023, includes most of Iowa's southeastern quadrant, including Davenport, Bettendorf, Burlington, and Iowa City. Previously, Miller-Meeks served as in the Iowa Senate from 2019 to 2021. She is a member of the Republican Party.</p>"}